  "title": "GCD and LCM accept 2^53 itself, not only values below it",
  "statement": "GCD accepts an operand equal to 2^53, and LCM accepts an operand or a result equal to 2^53. Only values above 2^53 give #NUM!.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "All recorded rows match after the boundary change: GCD 7,966 of 7,966 and LCM 7,967 of 7,967.",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": {
    "claim": "If a parameter to GCD is >=2^53, GCD returns the #NUM! error value. If LCM(a,b) >=2^53, LCM returns the #NUM! error value.",
